        4  The central government controls Somalia only partly. Militant groups occupy some parts of the country. Somaliland with the five north-western regions declared independence from Somalia in 1991. Despite of its de-facto independence, it is still internationally considered to be part of Somalia.
        5  Federal States
        6  The federal states (without Somaliland and without Banaadir that remains a region) consist of following pre-war regions:
        7  Galmudugh : Galgaduud and southern parts of Mudug.
        8  Hirshabelle : Hiiraan and Shabeellaha Dhexe.
        9  Jubaland : Gedo, Jubbada Dhexe and Jubbada Hoose.
       10  Koonfur Galbeed [South West] : Bakool, Bay and Shabeellaha Hoose.
       11  Puntland : Bari, Nugaal and northern parts of Mudug. It claims also the eastern districts of Somaliland.
       12  Pre-war Regions
       13  The population of the pre-war regions of Somalia according to latest estimates and calculations.
